ition":[[52,7]]}}}]],"pipeline":["stemmer"]}},{"documents":[],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[],"invertedIndex":[],"pipeline":["stemmer"]}},{"documents":[{"i":2,"t":"About Singlestep Singlestep is a personal engineering knowledge base built around interactive simulations. Instead of static diagrams and wall-of-text explanations, each non-trivial topic gets a small toy you can play with: toggle a setting, watch the system respond, build intuition by doing. Why this exists​ Most engineering content is one of two things: Reference docs that tell you what a thing does. Blog posts that tell you that someone learned a thing. There's a third option that doesn't get built often because it's expensive: interactive explanations that let you see exactly how a system behaves under different inputs. That's what this site is. How it's organized​ Docs — evergreen reference notes. Editable forever. Blog — dated posts about experiences, debugging stories, lessons. Playground — a gallery of every simulation, browsable on its own. Who I am​ (Replace this paragraph with a short bio before publishing.) Why this exists How it's organized Who I am","s":"About Singlestep","u":"/singlestep/about","h":"","p":1},{"i":6,"t":"This is the first post on Singlestep — a personal engineering knowledge base built around interactive simulations. The first hero demo is Redis read modes. Toggle between master and replica reads and watch where the requests go. It's the kind of thing that takes ten minutes to read about and three seconds to understand once you can see it. More to come — Kafka consumer rebalancing, cache eviction policies, transaction propagation. If a topic confused you the first time you learned it, that's exactly the kind of thing that gets a sim here.","s":"Welcome to Singlestep","u":"/singlestep/blog/welcome","h":"","p":5},{"i":8,"t":"Real entry points: Redis read modes — the V1 hero demo. Playground — browse every sim. Blog — dated posts. About — what this site is.","s":"Welcome","u":"/singlestep/docs/intro","h":"","p":7},{"i":10,"t":"Edit this list as the site grows. It's a cockpit for the author, not a TOC for visitors. Add your most-revisited pages here.","s":"Pinned (personal)","u":"/singlestep/docs/intro","h":"#pinned-personal","p":7},{"i":12,"t":"When you connect a Redis client to a cluster with replicas, you choose where reads go. The default — every read to the master — is safe but wastes the replicas. Routing reads to replicas trades a small amount of staleness for higher throughput and lower latency. Try the three modes below. Click Send GET a few times, then flip the toggle and notice which arrow lights up. to masterto r1to r2 Client Masterprimary Replica 1read replica Replica 2read replica masterreplicareplica-preferred Send GETAuto-fire 1500msReset idle serving request No events yet. Interact with the simulation above.","s":"Redis read modes","u":"/singlestep/docs/redis/read-modes","h":"","p":11},{"i":14,"t":"Mode Reads go to Writes go to Staleness window master Master only Master None replica Round-robin across replicas Master Replication lag replica-preferred Replicas if available, else master Master Replication lag","s":"What the modes mean","u":"/singlestep/docs/redis/read-modes","h":"#what-the-modes-mean","p":11},{"i":16,"t":"master — strong-read-after-write requirements. Session tokens, financial state, anything where a stale read is a bug. replica — read-heavy traffic that tolerates a few milliseconds of staleness. Product catalogs, feeds, leaderboards. replica-preferred — pragmatic default for most read-heavy services. Reads stay fast under normal conditions and fall back to master if all replicas are unhealthy.","s":"When to use which","u":"/singlestep/docs/redis/read-modes","h":"#when-to-use-which","p":11},{"i":18,"t":"Set mode to replica and turn on auto-fire. Notice that requests alternate between Replica 1 and Replica 2. Switch mode mid-flight to master. The next arrow snaps to the master. Compare the event log entries — replica reads are tagged green to highlight the trade-off you're making.","s":"Try this","u":"/singlestep/docs/redis/read-modes","h":"#try-this","p":11},{"i":20,"t":"Playground Every interactive simulation on the site, grouped by topic. Each one is embedded in a doc page that explains the concept — click through to learn the context. Caching Redis read modes Toggle between master/replica reads and watch traffic re-route in real time.","s":"Playground","u":"/singlestep/playground","h":"","p":19},{"i":22,"t":"Sandbox Not available in production builds.","s":"Sandbox","u":"/singlestep/sandbox","h":"","p":21}],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[["t/2",[0,1.454,1,0.936,2,1.454,3,0.936,4,0.936,5,1.454,6,0.936,7,0.877,8,0.877,9,1.259,10,1.259,11,1.259,12,1.259,13,1.259,14,1.956,15,0.936,16,1.259,17,1.259,18,0.723,19,0.936,20,0.936,21,1.259,22,1.259,23,0.565,24,0.936,25,0.723,26,1.956,27,1.259,28,0.936,29,1.259,30,1.259,31,1.956,32,1.259,33,0.936,34,1.259,35,1.784,36,1.956,37,1.454,38,1.956,39,1.454,40,1.124,41,1.259,42,0.723,43,1.259,44,1.259,45,1.259,46,1.259,47,1.379,48,1.259,49,0.936,50,0.936,51,1.259,52,0.936,53,1.259,54,1.259,55,0.936,56,0.565,57,1.956,58,0.461,59,1.259,60,1.259,61,0.936,62,1.259,63,0.936,64,1.259,65,1.259,66,1.259,67,1.259,68,0.723,69,1.259,70,1.259,71,1.259,72,1.259,73,1.259,74,1.259,75,1.259,76,1.259]],["t/6",[0,1.22,1,1.22,2,1.22,3,1.22,4,1.22,5,1.22,6,1.22,7,0.736,8,0.736,18,0.943,19,1.22,23,0.736,25,0.943,35,1.775,40,0.943,42,0.943,47,0.943,49,1.22,50,1.22,55,1.22,58,0.459,77,2.814,78,1.22,79,1.22,80,0.736,81,0.541,82,0.433,83,0.943,84,0.571,85,0.571,86,0.943,87,0.943,88,2.387,89,1.64,90,1.64,91,1.64,92,1.22,93,1.64,94,1.64,95,1.64,96,1.64,97,1.64,98,1.64,99,1.64,100,1.64,101,1.22,102,1.64,103,1.64,104,1.64,105,1.64,106,1.64,107,0.943,108,1.22,109,1.22]],["t/8",[39,1.863,40,1.44,56,1.124,58,0.71,63,1.863,68,1.44,78,1.863,79,1.863,80,1.124,81,0.481,82,0.661,108,1.863,110,1.863,111,1.863,112,2.50